  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district (Aug 31 FYE). Governmental lines use the Totals Governmental Funds column (p7-9); beginning/ending cash = total fund balance 1,530,629 / 1,872,140 (p9), equal to cash plus cash at county treasurers. Transfers out 100,614 (General Fund 118,907 less 18,293 transfer to Activities Fund eliminated by Adjustments column); transfers in total 0 after elimination. 'Other' receipts (237,465) and 'Other Support Services' (299,601) were split using the fund columns printed on the same lines (Activities Fund holds 228,514 receipts and 251,501 disbursements; Depreciation Fund 48,100). State Categorical and Federal Programs mapped to instruction. School Nutrition is the only proprietary fund (business-type): receipts are the sum of printed lines (operating 133,504 + interest 138 = 133,642), measure = cash since cash basis (cash 43,656 equals net position). Detail: general fund budget schedule used (more detailed than the statement); fund schedules p15-19 for the other funds; the Activities Fund club-by-club schedule (p20-21) was not recorded to avoid double counting with the Activities Fund schedule. Detail transfers: General Fund 8000 Transfers -118,907 (includes 100,614 to nutrition and 18,293 to activities); schedule totals that include transfers carry includes other financing. Budget columns are 'Original and Final'. No liabilities on the cash-basis net position statement. Read pages 1-21 of 21."
